DailerApps entrusts personal information processing tasks as follows: Recipient of entrustment (trustee): App Store Contents of entrusted tasks: Purchase and payment processing Period of entrustment: Managed by App Store
If the content of entrusted tasks or the trustee changes, we will promptly disclose it through this privacy policy.
Article 6 (Procedures and Methods of Destruction of Personal Information)

DailerApps destroys personal information without delay when the retention period of personal information has expired, the processing purpose has been achieved, etc.
The procedures and methods of destruction are as follows: DailerApps selects personal information that has become unnecessary and obtains approval from DailerApps' personal information protection manager before destroying it. Electronic files are destroyed using a technical method that cannot regenerate records.
Article 7 (Rights and Obligations of Information Subjects and Methods of Exercising Rights)

Data subjects may exercise the right to access, correct, delete, or suspend processing of their personal information with respect to DailerApps at any time.
The exercise of rights under paragraph 1 can be done through written, electronic mail, facsimile, etc. in accordance with Article 41(1) of the Personal Information Protection Act, and DailerApps will take immediate action.
Rights under paragraph 1 may be exercised through a legal representative or agent of the data subject. In this case, a power of attorney pursuant to Form 11 of the Enforcement Regulations of the Personal Information Protection Act must be submitted.
The right to access and request correction or deletion of personal information may be restricted under Articles 35(4), 37(2), and other provisions of the Personal Information Protection Act.
In cases where personal information cannot be deleted as it is specified by other laws, access, and correction requests may not be accepted.
DailerApps verifies whether the requester of rights under paragraph 1 is the data subject or a legal representative and takes action accordingly.
Article 8 (Measures for Securing the Safety of Personal Information) DailerApps takes the following measures to ensure the safety of personal information: Establishment and enforcement of an internal management plan DailerApps establishes and enforces an internal management plan to ensure the safe processing of personal information. Minimization and education of personal information handling staff DailerApps designates personnel to handle personal information and restricts them to a minimum for proper management of personal information.

Article 9 (Installation, Operation, and Refusal of Automatic Personal Information Collection Devices) DailerApps does not use "cookies" to store and retrieve user information.

Article 10 (Personal Information Protection Manager)

DailerApps is responsible for overall management of personal information processing and has appointed a personal information protection manager as follows: • Contact information for the personal information protection manager: customer@dailerapps.com
Data subjects may contact the personal information protection manager or the relevant department at any time regarding inquiries, complaints, damage relief, etc., related to personal information processing by DailerApps. DailerApps will respond promptly.
Article 11 (Department in Charge of Processing Requests for Access to Personal Information) Data subjects can request access to personal information under Article 35 of the Personal Information Protection Act to the following department: DailerApps will make efforts to ensure that requests for access to personal information are processed promptly.

